Markdown links can use short references:

┌──────────┐
│          │
│   Docs   │
│          │
└──────────┘

Read [the Topos repository](#topos)

The same [reference](#topos) can be reused.

An [unresolved reference](#missing) stays ordinary text.

Direct [URLs](https://example.com) work when source width is not a concern.

:legend w=30
Docs: href="https://example.com"
#topos: href="https://github.com/alexdrel/topos"
